Answer the PCRF's RAR in ims_qos and act on lost media bearers.

TS 29.214 4.4.6.2: when the AF receives a RAR "it shall acknowledge the
command by sending an RAA". ims_qos returned nothing for a RAR, so the PCRF
retransmitted and timed out, and a lost or released bearer was ignored: the
call went on without its media.

Answer every RAR at once: 2001, or 5002 DIAMETER_UNKNOWN_SESSION_ID for an
Rx session we do not have.

Specific-Action INDICATION_OF_LOSS_OF_BEARER or _RELEASE_OF_BEARER on a
media session names the affected media components in its Flows AVPs. TS
24.229 5.2.8.1.1 (session being established) and 5.2.8.1.2 (established):
if no SIP message removes that media within an operator defined time, the
P-CSCF releases the session. Remember those components; an SDP offer/answer
that drops them (port 0 or no m= line) clears them, as does a RAR with
INDICATION_OF_RECOVERY_OF_BEARER or _ESTABLISHMENT_OF_BEARER for them. A
1 s timer terminates the Rx sessions that still have such components at
their deadline, the new bearer_release_wait modparam (default 5 s). The
dialog is then released as after an ASR: when the STA arrives, if
terminate_dialog_on_rx_failure is set, with early_qosrelease_reason or
confirmed_qosrelease_headers.

On the signalling path session (4.4.6.3) the AF may terminate it: do so
without waiting, which goes on as before for a terminated signalling
session (the contact is deregistered when delete_contact_on_rx_failure is
set).

